    rdfs:label "Evidence for Bismuth used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BISMUTH"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "An alloy of 1 bismuth, 2 tin, and 1 lead, is employed as a soft solder by the pewterers; and the same has been proposed as a bath for tempering steel instruments."@en ;
